#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/scripts

# The whole site. Owns the transport and nothing else: each domain is detached
# and brings its own routes, so this file never learns what a thread or a board
# is.
#
# Order matters twice over.
#
# The LANDING PAGE is added first. HttpServer::ResolvePath walks typed children
# in the order they were added and takes the first match, and chess_web.etcs's
# own board_page also answers "/" -- so whichever is attached first owns it.
# Adding landing here, before either lobby is detached, is what makes that
# deterministic rather than a function of which script ran first.
#
# The lobbies are detached AFTER Start. Each one spawns `web` by that same name,
# and spawn_entity retargets a pending name already bound to a live entity of
# the same module and tag -- PersistentNames is process-scope, not per-script --
# so they find THIS server instead of minting a second one and failing to bind
# 8080. Their own Start calls are no-ops: StartConcrete returns false when a
# manager already exists. Their duplicate FileHtmlPage children are harmless
# for the same first-match reason, just redundant.

NetworkProvider
HttpServer web
spawn web
SetPort 8080

web.add(StaticHtmlPage landing)
SetHtmlFromFile ./www/static/index.html
context NetworkProvider::HttpServer web

# Everything else is disk layout as url layout: /chess.html, /forum.html,
# /whitepaper.html. One page type, no per-document entity, and adding a
# document is copying a file rather than editing this script.
web.add(FileHtmlPage tree)
LoadFromDisk ./www
ListPaths tree
context NetworkProvider::HttpServer web

# The tar-pit: a self-registering, gate-level filter that catches
# bot-scan-shaped paths (.env, wp-admin, .php, ...) and answers them with a
# deliberately slow 404 instead of routing them anywhere real -- see
# TarpitNode.h for why it lives here as its own entity rather than a flag on
# HttpServer or ConnectionManager. Spawned as a PEER of web, not a child of
# it: it is a consumer of web's own gate, the same relationship HttpServer's
# own default Serve registration has, not an owned page.
#
# LoadDefaultTarpitPatterns is redundant with TarpitNode's own constructor
# (which loads the same list) -- called explicitly anyway so the pattern
# list is a visible line in this script rather than an invisible default,
# matching every other configurable thing here.
#
# FULLY QUALIFIED, and it has to be. A bare `TarpitNode tarpit` only reads
# as a tag selection when the context has no tag yet -- which is why
# `HttpServer web` works at the top of this script. Here a tag IS already
# in context (web, from the line above), so the same shape parses as an
# ACTION named TarpitNode with the payload `tarpit`, dispatched against
# HttpServer. That fails with a logged "Tag: HttpServer does not provide
# requested action: TarpitNode" and leaves the context untouched -- so the
# `spawn` on the next line spawns another HTTPSERVER named `tarpit`, and
# every @tarpit below resolves to it. The result is a filtered gate-level
# consumer whose Filter and Request actions do not exist, which declines
# every connection and tarpits nothing.
context NetworkProvider::TarpitNode tarpit
spawn tarpit
LoadDefaultTarpitPatterns

# AddHandler @tarpit Request @tarpit Filter registers the tar-pit as a
# FILTERED gate-level consumer -- ConnectionManager::dispatchToSubscribers
# tries every filtered subscriber before falling back to unfiltered ones, so
# a scan-shaped path is caught here and never reaches web's own Serve.
#
# AddHandler @web Serve is NOT redundant with what Start does automatically
# -- it looks identical to the implicit default (StartConcrete registers
# web's own Serve when handlers_ is empty), but the moment ANY handler is
# added, handlers_ stops being empty and that implicit default is skipped.
# Without this second line, the tar-pit would be the ONLY registered
# consumer and every real request would find no unfiltered fallback and be
# dropped. Declaring it explicitly here is what keeps that fallback alive
# now that a filtered handler exists at all.
context NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
AddHandler @tarpit Request @tarpit Filter
AddHandler @web Serve

Start
IsStarted

detach chess_lobby.etcs
detach forum_lobby.etcs

# http://localhost:8080/
